                        "entry_id": "cd059803-19e5-39df-81b9-43c1a9a69b23",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The quality of being material; having a physical existence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2b9ab4a-ffd5-46ef-bcac-5ba423842e47",
                                "sense_id": "2a22f5d4-0491-3c20-adcd-282f5772654e",
                                "text": "This deed accomplished, life no longer suffers hopelessly under the terrible mutilations of ubiquitous disaster, battered by time, hideous throughout space; but with its horror visible still, its cries of anguish still tumultuous, it becomes penetrated by an all-suffusing, all-sustaining love, and a knowledge of its own unconquered power. Something of the light that blazes invisible within the abysses of its normally opaque materiality breaks forth, with an increasing uproar."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8cf44dcf-c98e-4f5a-a1ef-99d0790f92e8",
                                "sense_id": "2a22f5d4-0491-3c20-adcd-282f5772654e",
                                "text": "According to Judd, in his polemical statement of aesthetic purpose \"Specific Objects,\" written the year he created Untitled, the intransigent materiality of his nonallusive objects would provide a \"credible\" experience for viewers, free from any external connotations."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
